          "insert": "Process Guardians"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-process-guardians-evented-process-guardian-2": {
      "id": "b-25-process-guardians-evented-process-guardian-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Evented process guardians, babysit wrapper semantics, health incidents, and recovery policy."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-process-guardians-a-process-guardian-is-an-3": {
      "id": "b-25-process-guardians-a-process-guardian-is-an-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A process guardian is an evented safety layer around the decomp system process.\nIt is not a scheduler, worker, or always-on reasoning agent. It sleeps while the\nsystem process runs, wakes when the process exits or reports a health incident,\nrecords the incident packet, runs deterministic recovery, and then restarts the\nsystem when policy allows."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-process-guardians-process-stack-4": {
      "id": "b-25-process-guardians-process-stack-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Process Stack"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-process-guardians-text-5": {
      "id": "b-25-process-guardians-text-5",
      "type": "process-outline",
      "props": {
        "steps": [
          {
            "text": "Guardian process",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "watches process exit",
                "kind": "note"
              },
              {
                "text": "records health incidents",
                "kind": "note"
              },
              {
                "text": "recovers failed claims",
                "kind": "note"
              },
              {
                "text": "restarts system process",
                "kind": "note"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Decomp system process",
            "steps": [
              {
                "text": "Trigger actor",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "scheduler tick, fill worker slots, sleep",
                    "kind": "note"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Scheduler",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "epoch intent",
                    "kind": "note"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "text": "Worker sessions",
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "claimed work",
                    "kind": "note"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-25-process-guardians-the-run-loop-lives-insid-6": {
      "id": "b-25-process-guardians-the-run-loop-lives-insid-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The run loop lives inside the decomp system process. It advances durable run\nstate by running deterministic scheduler ticks and realizing worker slots.\nThe guardian wraps that process boundary and handles liveness, crash recovery,\nand incident artifacts."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
